npx lint-staged --no-stash

# --no-stash: lint-staged's default flow stashes unstaged changes before
# running formatters so it can restore them if something fails. That stash
# step (`git stash create`/`store`) turned out to be unreliable in at least
# one dev environment on this project (a FUSE-mounted repo) -- it failed
# with a generic "git error" even though prettier itself ran fine once the
# stash step was skipped. We don't rely on partial-hunk staging in this
# workflow (files are staged whole), so the safety net --no-stash disables
# isn't something we lean on anyway.

# lint-staged runs prettier per-file, but ESLint's flat config lives inside
# each workspace (server/eslint.config.js, client/eslint.config.js) — there
# is no root eslint.config.js, so running `eslint` on a repo-root-relative
# path fails to find a config. Lint each workspace properly instead of
# trying to make lint-staged's per-file eslint invocation workspace-aware.
npm run lint --workspace server
npm run lint --workspace client
